@node Formal semantics
@section Formal semantics

This section provides a formal denotational semantics for the primitive
expressions of Scheme and selected built-in procedures.  The concepts
and notation used here are described in @cite{Denotational Semantics:
The Scott-Strachey Approach to Programming Language
Theory}@footnote{@value{refScottStrachey}}; the definition of
dynamic-wind is taken from @cite{How to Add Threads to a Sequential
Language Without Getting Tangled
Up}@footnote{@value{refHowToAddThreads}}.  The notation is summarized
below:

@indentedblock
@multitable @columnfractions .15 .85
@item @angle{@value{defdots}} @tab sequence formation
@item 𝑠 ↓ 𝑘 @tab 𝑘th member of the sequence 𝑠 (1-based)
@item @hashchar{}𝑠 @tab length of sequence 𝑠
@item 𝑠 § 𝑡 @tab concatenation of sequences 𝑠 and 𝑡
@item 𝑠 † 𝑘 @tab drop the first 𝑘 members of sequence 𝑠

@item 𝑡 @arrow{} 𝑎, 𝑏 @tab
McCarthy conditional @quotedbl{if 𝑡 then 𝑎 else 𝑏}

@item 𝜌[𝑥/𝑖] @tab substitution @quotedbl{𝜌 with 𝑥 for 𝑖}
@item 𝑥 in @t{D} @tab injection of 𝑥 into domain @t{D}
@item 𝑥 | @t{D} @tab projection of 𝑥 to domain @t{D}
@end multitable
@end indentedblock

The reason that expression continuations take sequences of values
instead of single values is to simplify the formal treatment of
procedure calls and multiple return values.

The boolean flag associated with pairs, vectors, and strings will be
true for mutable objects and false for immutable objects.

The order of evaluation within a call is unspecified.  We mimic that
here by applying arbitrary permutations @define{permute} and
@define{unpermute}, which must be inverses, to the arguments in a call
before and after they are evaluated.  This is not quite right since it
suggests, incorrectly, that the order of evaluation is constant
throughout a program (for any given number of arguments), but it is a
closer approximation to the intended semantics than a left-to-right
evaluation would be.

The storage allocator new is implementation-dependent, but it must obey
the following axiom: if
@nobr{@i{new}@inlinefmtifelse{html,@U{2009},@tie{}}𝜎 ∈ @t{L}}, then
@nobr{σ (@i{new}@inlinefmtifelse{html,@U{2009},@tie{}}𝜎 ∣ @t{L})↓2 =
@i{false}}.

The definition of 𝜘 is omitted because an accurate definition of 𝜘 would
com@value{shy}plicate the semantics without being very interesting.

If P is a program in which all variables are defined before being
referenced or assigned, then the meaning of P is

@display
𝜀⟦@t{((@syntax{lambda} (@r{I*}) @r{P′}) @angle{undefined} @value{defdots})}⟧
@end display

where I* is the sequence of variables defined in P, P′ is the sequence
of expressions obtained by replacing every definition in P by an
assignment, @angle{undefined} is an expression that evaluates to
undefined, and 𝜀 is the semantic function that assigns meaning to
expressions.

@node Abstract syntax
@subsection Abstract syntax
@indentedblock
@table @asis
@item K ∈ Con
constants, including quotations
@item I ∈ Ide
identifiers (variables)
@item E ∈ Exp
expressions
@item Γ ∈ Com = Exp
commands
@end table
@end indentedblock

@example grammar
@r{Exp} @longarrow{} @r{K} | @r{I} | (@r{@parzero{E}} @r{E*})
    | (lambda (@r{I*}) @r{Γ*} @r{@parzero{E}})
    | (lambda (@r{I*} . @r{I}) @r{Γ*} @r{@parzero{E}})
    | (lambda @r{I} @r{Γ*} @r{@parzero{E}})
    | (if @r{@parzero{E}} @r{@parI{E}} @r{@parII{E}}) | (if @r{@parzero{E}} @r{@parI{E}})
    | (set! @r{I} @r{E})
@end example

@node Domain equations
@subsection Abstract syntax
@multitable @columnfractions .03 .03 .04 .63 .27
@item 𝛼 @tab ∈ @tab @t{L} @tab @tab locations
@item 𝜈 @tab ∈ @tab @t{N} @tab @tab natural numbers
@item @tab @tab @t{T} @tab = @{@i{false, true}@} @tab booleans
@item @tab @tab @t{Q} @tab @tab symbols
@item @tab @tab @t{H} @tab @tab characters
@item @tab @tab @t{R} @tab @tab numbers
@item @tab @tab @t{@parp{E}} @tab = @t{L} × @t{L} × @t{T} @tab pairs
@item @tab @tab @t{@parv{E}} @tab = @t{L*} × @t{T} @tab vectors
@item @tab @tab @t{@pars{E}} @tab = @t{L*} × @t{T} @tab strings

@item @tab @tab @t{M} @tab
= @{@i{false, true, null, undefined, unspecified}@}
@tab miscellaneous

@item 𝜙 @tab ∈ @tab @t{F} @tab
= @t{L} × (@t{E}* @arrow{} @t{P} @arrow{} @t{K} @arrow{} @t{C})
@tab procedure values

@item 𝜖 @tab ∈ @tab @t{E} @tab
= @t{Q} + @t{H} + @t{R} + @t{@parp{E}} + @t{@parv{E}} + @t{@pars{E}} +
@t{M} + @t{F}
@tab expressed values

@item 𝜎 @tab ∈ @tab @t{S} @tab = @t{L} @arrow{} (@t{E} × @t{T}) @tab stores
@item 𝜌 @tab ∈ @tab @t{U} @tab = Ide @arrow{} @t{L} @tab environments
@item 𝜃 @tab ∈ @tab @t{C} @tab = @t{S} @arrow{} @t{A} @tab command conts
@item 𝜅 @tab ∈ @tab @t{K} @tab = @t{E}* @arrow{} @t{C} @tab expression conts
@item @tab @tab @t{A} @tab @tab answers
@item @tab @tab @t{X} @tab @tab errors
@item 𝜔 @tab ∈ @tab @t{P} @tab
= (@t{F} × @t{F} × @t{P}) + @{@i{root}@}
@tab dynamic points
@end multitable

@node Semantic functions
@subsection Semantic functions

@multitable @columnfractions .03 .03 0.94
@item 𝜘 @tab : @tab Con @arrow{} @t{E}

@item 𝜀 @tab : @tab
Exp @arrow{} @t{U} @arrow{} @t{P} @arrow{} @t{K} @arrow{} @t{C}

@item 𝜀* @tab : @tab
Exp* @arrow{} @t{U} @arrow{} @t{P} @arrow{} @t{K} @arrow{} @t{C}

@item 𝐶* @tab : @tab
Com* @arrow{} @t{U} @arrow{} @t{P} @arrow{} @t{C} @arrow{} @t{C}
@end multitable

Definition of 𝜘 deliberately omitted.

@display
𝜀⟦K⟧ = 𝜆𝜌𝜔𝜅 . @i{send}(𝜘⟦K⟧)𝜅
@end display

@display
𝜀⟦I⟧ = 𝜆𝜌𝜔𝜅 . @i{hold}(@i{lookup} 𝜌 I)
@t{               }(@i{single}(𝜆𝜖 . 𝜖 = @i{undefined} @arrow{}
@t{                             }@i{wrong} @quotedbl{undefined variable},
@t{                           }@i{send} 𝜖 𝜅))
@end display

@display
𝜀⟦@t{@U{0028}}@parzero{E} E*@t{@U{0029}}⟧ =
@t{ }𝜆𝜌𝜔𝜅 . 𝜀*(@i{permute}(@angle{@parzero{E}} § E*))
@t{         }𝜌
@t{         }𝜔
@t{         }(𝜆𝜖* . ((𝜆𝜖* . @i{applicate} (𝜖* ↓ 1)(𝜖* † 1) 𝜔𝜅)
@t{               }(@i{unpermute} 𝜖*)))
@end display

@c 𝜔′𝜅′ . #𝜖* = #I* @arrow{}
@c                        @i{tievals}(𝜆𝛼* . (𝜆𝜌′ . 𝐶
